<style>
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
    --gradient-background: {% if section.settings.gradient_background != blank %}{{ section.settings.gradient_background }}{% else %}{{ section.settings.color_background }}{% endif %};
    --color-background: {{ section.settings.color_background.rgb }};
    --color-foreground: {{ section.settings.color_text.rgb }};
  }
  .onrepeat-currency-pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 3px;
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground) / 0.28);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground) / 0.06);
  }
  .onrepeat-currency-pill__side {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    min-height: 38px;
    padding: 0 16px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground) / 0.72);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .onrepeat-currency-pill__side.is-active {
    background: #5c1011;
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: default;
  }
  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
     Footer identity band. `position: relative` is load-bearing: .section
     paints via an absolutely-positioned ::before with no negative z-index
     (theme.css:4852) that covers static children. It is also
     pointer-events:none, so hit-testing cannot detect the occlusion — the
     failure is invisible to elementFromPoint and only shows in a screenshot.
     The background repaint is belt-and-braces for the same reason.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
  .onrepeat-fx {
    position: relative;
    background: var(--gradient-background);
    background-color: rgb(var(--color-background));
  }
  .onrepeat-fx__inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(20px, 3.4vw, 30px);
    /* The copyright strip below brings its own top padding, so this end value
       is intentionally lighter than the start. */
    padding-block: clamp(30px, 4.8vw, 46px) clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 22px);
  }

  /* Payment marks */
  .onrepeat-pay {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(11px, 1.6vw, 15px);
    width: 100%;
  }
  .onrepeat-pay__label {
    font-size: 9.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground) / 0.42);
  }
  .onrepeat-pay__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .onrepeat-pay__item {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 5px;
    width: 56px;
    height: 34px;
    padding: 6px 8px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: #fff;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.09);
  }
  .onrepeat-pay__item--tight { padding: 6px 9px; }
  .onrepeat-pay__item--cod {
    width: auto;
    min-width: 56px;
    padding-inline: 9px;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .onrepeat-pay__item--cod img { width: 17px; height: 17px; flex: none; }
  .onrepeat-pay__item img {
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 100%;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Seller identity */
  .onrepeat-legal {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    width: 100%;
    padding-block-start: clamp(20px, 3vw, 26px);
    border-block-start: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground) / 0.11);
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .onrepeat-legal p { margin: 0; }
  .onrepeat-legal__name {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground) / 0.88);
  }
  @media screen and (max-width: 519px) {
    .onrepeat-pay__item { width: 52px; height: 32px; }
  }
  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    .onrepeat-pay__row { gap: 9px; }
    .onrepeat-pay__item { width: 60px; height: 36px; }
    .onrepeat-legal__name { font-size: 13px; }
  }
  .onrepeat-currency-pill__side:not(.is-active):hover {
    color: rgb(var(--color-foreground));
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground) / 0.09);
  }
  .onrepeat-currency-pill__side:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground));
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .onrepeat-currency-pill__flag {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    /* Stacked layout: the pill reads as a storefront control, not small print —
       it sits above the copyright line, matching the approved design. */
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .localization {
      order: -1;
    }
  }
</style>

{%- comment -%}
  The identity band lives INSIDE the parallax .section, as the theme intends — one section, one
  transform, so nothing slides against anything else while the footer reveals on scroll.

  It needs its own .onrepeat-fx wrapper for one reason: .section paints through an absolutely
  positioned ::before with no negative z-index (theme.css:4852), which covers static children.
  Anything added here must be positioned to paint above it. That overlay is also
  pointer-events:none, so elementFromPoint cannot see the occlusion — this bug is invisible to
  hit-testing and only shows up in a screenshot. .onrepeat-fx and .onrepeat-legal both carry
  `position: relative` for exactly this. Do not remove it.

  The band is now the brand line alone. The store location, CIN and GSTIN that used to sit under
  it were removed at the merchant's request; none of that disclosure has left the site, it just
  no longer appears in the footer. It still lives in:

    templates/page.llms.liquid:40-46          CIN, GSTIN and principal place of business
    snippets/schema-sitewide.liquid:33-42     both identifiers as Organization JSON-LD
    templates/product.json:116                the Manufactured & Marketed by block on every PDP
    the Terms of Service page                 the registered office

  So the MCA and GST registries still resolve THE ONREPEAT CLOTHING™ to SUNYE ATTIRE PRIVATE LIMITED
  for anyone who checks, and the structured data search engines read is untouched.

  The line reads THE ONREPEAT CLOTHING™ rather than the registered entity name: the shopper knows the
  brand. ™ not ® — the marks are applied for, not yet registered.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="section{% if section.settings.divider %} section--divider{% endif %}{% if section.settings.rounded %} section--rounded{% endif %}"{% if section.settings.enable_parallax %} is="footer-parallax"{% endif %}>
  <div class="onrepeat-fx">
    <div class="onrepeat-fx__inner page-width{% if section.settings.full_width %} page-width--full{% endif %} w-full">
      {%- render 'onrepeat-payment-icons', section: section -%}

      {%- if section.settings.show_legal_entity -%}
        <div class="onrepeat-legal">
          <p class="onrepeat-legal__name">THE ONREPEAT CLOTHING&trade;</p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-copyright page-width{% if section.settings.full_width %} page-width--full{% endif %} w-full flex flex-col items-center justify-between gap-4 lg:gap-0 lg:flex-row relative">
    <div class="rte credits text-center">
      {%- liquid
        if section.settings.show_copyright
          echo '&copy;&nbsp;'
          echo 'now' | date: '%Y'
          echo '&nbsp;'
          echo shop.name
          if section.settings.copyright_text != blank
            echo '&nbsp;'
            echo section.settings.copyright_text
          endif
          echo '.&nbsp;'
        endif
      -%}
      <a href="https://www.softpipersolutions.com" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" class="reversed-link">Powered by Softpiper Solutions</a>
      {%- if section.settings.show_policy -%}
        <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 justify-center lg:justify-start">
          {%- for policy in shop.policies -%}
            {%- if policy != blank -%}
              <li>
                <small>
                  <a href="{{ policy.url }}" class="block reversed-link">{{ policy.title }}</a>
                </small>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- liquid
      if section.settings.enable_language_selector and localization.available_languages.size > 1
        assign enable_language_selector = true
      endif
      if section.settings.enable_country_selector and localization.available_countries.size > 1
        assign enable_country_selector = true
      endif
    -%}
    {%- if enable_language_selector or enable_country_selector -%}
      <div class="localization flex items-center justify-center flex-col md:flex-row">
        {%- if enable_language_selector -%}
          <div class="grid gap-2">
            {%- form 'localization', id: 'localization_language_form_footer', class: 'localization__form flex items-center relative', is: 'localization-form' -%}
              <label class="sr-only" for="LocalizationLanguageFormFooter">
                {{- 'localization.language_label' | t -}}
              </label>
              {%- render 'icon', icon: 'language', size: 'xs', class: 'stroke-1 absolute pointer-events-none' -%}
              <select class="localization__item cursor-pointer leading-tight w-full" name="locale_code" id="LocalizationLanguageFormFooter">
                {%- for language in localization.available_languages -%}
                  <option value="{{ language.iso_code }}"{% if language.iso_code == localization.language.iso_code %} selected{% endif %}>
                    {{- language.endonym_name | capitalize -}}
                  </option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
              {%- render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-down', size: 'xs', class: 'absolute pointer-events-none' -%}
            {%- endform -%}
            <noscript>
              <button class="button button--primary button--small w-full" type="submit" form="localization_language_form_footer">
                {{- 'localization.update_language' | t -}}
              </button>
            </noscript>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if enable_country_selector and localization.available_countries.size == 2 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Exactly two markets (India + United States today): a two-sided pill
            on the REAL localization form. Buttons carry the country_code, the
            active side is disabled so it cannot resubmit, and the whole thing
            works with zero JS — the form tag itself provides form_type, utf8
            and the _method=put override Shopify's /localization route needs.
            Switching market context is coherent even before USD display is
            enabled: prices simply follow the market's price list.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- form 'localization', id: 'localization_country_form_footer', class: 'onrepeat-currency-pill' -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="return_to" value="{{ request.path }}">
            {%- liquid
              comment
                The label CANNOT come from country.currency. This store presents
                only INR, so Shopify reports the United States market's currency
                as INR too — the pill rendered "🇺🇸 ₹ INR" on both sides, which is
                the exact confusion this feature exists to remove. The US side is
                labelled from the display layer instead, and only claims dollars
                when USD display is actually on; with the feature off it names the
                region, because that market still charges INR.
              endcomment
              assign pill_rate = settings.usd_inr_rate | default: 0 | round
              assign pill_usd_on = false
              if settings.usd_display_enabled and pill_rate > 0
                assign pill_usd_on = true
              endif
            -%}
            {%- for country in localization.available_countries -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign is_current = false
                if country.iso_code == localization.country.iso_code
                  assign is_current = true
                endif

                assign pill_label = country.currency.symbol | append: ' ' | append: country.currency.iso_code
                if country.iso_code == 'US'
                  if pill_usd_on
                    assign pill_label = '$ USD'
                  else
                    assign pill_label = 'US'
                  endif
                elsif country.iso_code == 'IN'
                  assign pill_label = '₹ INR'
                endif
              -%}
              <button
                type="{% if is_current %}button{% else %}submit{% endif %}"
                class="onrepeat-currency-pill__side{% if is_current %} is-active{% endif %}"
                {% if is_current %}aria-current="true" disabled{% else %}name="country_code" value="{{ country.iso_code }}"{% endif %}
                aria-label="{% if is_current %}Showing prices for {% else %}Switch to {% endif %}{{ country.name | escape }} ({{ pill_label }})"
              >
                {%- if country.iso_code == 'IN' -%}
                  <span class="onrepeat-currency-pill__flag" aria-hidden="true">&#127470;&#127475;</span>
                {%- elsif country.iso_code == 'US' -%}
                  <span class="onrepeat-currency-pill__flag" aria-hidden="true">&#127482;&#127480;</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                {{ pill_label }}
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endform -%}
        {%- elsif enable_country_selector -%}
          <div class="grid gap-2">
            {%- form 'localization', id: 'localization_country_form_footer', class: 'localization__form flex items-center relative', is: 'localization-form' -%}
              <label class="sr-only" for="LocalizationCountryFormFooter">
                {{- 'localization.country_label' | t -}}
              </label>
              {%- render 'icon', icon: 'currency', size: 'xs', class: 'stroke-1 absolute pointer-events-none' -%}
              <select class="localization__item cursor-pointer leading-tight w-full" name="country_code" id="LocalizationCountryFormFooter">
                {%- for country in localization.available_countries -%}
                  <option value="{{ country.iso_code }}"{% if country.iso_code == localization.country.iso_code %} selected{% endif %}>
                    {{- country.name }} ({{ country.currency.iso_code }} {{ country.currency.symbol }})
                  </option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
              {%- render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-down', size: 'xs', class: 'absolute pointer-events-none' -%}
            {%- endform -%}
            <noscript>
              <button class="button button--primary button--small w-full" type="submit" form="localization_country_form_footer">
                {{- 'localization.update_country' | t -}}
              </button>
            </noscript>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Shopify's own payment row is kept for stores on Shopify Payments, but it renders nothing here:
      shop.enabled_payment_types is only populated for Shopify Payments and this store checks out
      through Razorpay, so the `unless … == empty` guard has been short-circuiting and the footer has
      shown no payment marks at all. onrepeat-payment-icons carries the marks that actually apply,
      including UPI and RuPay, which Shopify's payment_type_svg_tag filter does not ship.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.show_payment_icons -%}
      {%- unless shop.enabled_payment_types == empty -%}
        <ul class="payment-icons{% if section.settings.monochrome_payment_icons %} payment-icons--gray{% endif %} flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2 xl:gap-3">
          {%- for type in shop.enabled_payment_types -%}
            <li>
              {{- type | payment_type_svg_tag -}}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.footer-copyright.name",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Payment methods",
      "info": "Shopify's own payment icons only work on Shopify Payments, so they render nothing on this store. These are real brand artwork bundled with the theme and include UPI, RuPay and COD, which Shopify does not provide. Tick only what Razorpay is actually configured to accept — an icon for a method that fails at checkout is a broken promise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "pay_heading",
      "default": "Payments accepted",
      "label": "Row label",
      "info": "Leave blank to hide the label."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "pay_upi", "default": true, "label": "UPI" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "pay_visa", "default": true, "label": "Visa" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "pay_mastercard", "default": true, "label": "Mastercard" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "pay_rupay", "default": true, "label": "RuPay" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "pay_amex", "default": true, "label": "American Express" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "pay_applepay", "default": true, "label": "Apple Pay" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "pay_paypal", "default": true, "label": "PayPal" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "pay_cod", "default": true, "label": "Cash on delivery (COD)" },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Seller identity"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_legal_entity",
      "default": true,
      "label": "Show legal entity details",
      "info": "Shows the brand line THE ONREPEAT CLOTHING™ above the copyright. The store location, CIN and GSTIN that used to sit here have been removed from the footer; they remain on the LLMs page, in the Organization structured data, on every product page and in the Terms of Service."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.header__language_selector.content",
      "info": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.header__language_selector.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_language_selector",
      "label": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.enable_language_selector.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.header__country_selector.content",
      "info": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.header__country_selector.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_country_selector",
      "label": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.enable_country_selector.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.header__policy.content",
      "info": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.header__policy.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_policy",
      "label": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.show_policy.label",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.header__payment_methods.content"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_payment_icons",
      "label": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.show_payment_icons.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "monochrome_payment_icons",
      "label": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.monochrome_payment_icons.label",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.header__additional_content.content"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_copyright",
      "label": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.show_copyright.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "copyright_text",
      "label": "t:sections.footer-copyright.settings.copyright_text.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.global.settings.header__colors.content",
      "info": "t:sections.global.settings.header__colors.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "color_text",
      "label": "t:sections.global.settings.color_text.label",
      "default": "#ffffff"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "color_background",
      "label": "t:sections.global.settings.color_background.label",
      "default": "#171717"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_background",
      "id": "gradient_background",
      "label": "t:sections.global.settings.gradient_background.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.global.settings.header__section.content"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "divider",
      "label": "t:sections.global.settings.divider.label",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "full_width",
      "label": "t:sections.global.settings.full_width.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "rounded",
      "default": false,
      "label": "t:sections.global.settings.rounded.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_parallax",
      "label": "t:sections.global.settings.enable_parallax.label",
      "default": true
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "groups": [
      "footer"
    ]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
